{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityIContentDecomposition","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityIContentDecomposition","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Intervals"],"declarations":66,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.idB_verified_le12_prop","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.idB_verified_le12_prop","kind":"theorem","line":992,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L992-L997","doc":"**Identity (B), propositional form for `n ≤ 12`**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.idB_verified_le12","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.idB_verified_le12","kind":"theorem","line":982,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L982-L990","doc":"**Identity (B), faithfully stated and machine-checked (sorry-free).**\n`Σ_{λ⊢n} dim(λ)² · Σ_{c∈λ} c(c)² = n!·binom(n,2)`, verified by kernel `decide` for **all\npartitions `n ≤ 12`** — refuting the earlier note that (B) \"cannot even be stated faithfully\nwithout `ℂ[S_n]` infrastructure\".  With `dim_validated_le12` (which certifies the dimension)\nthis is a complete, self-contained verification of the Plancherel content-square mean on\n`n ≤ 12`; the general-`n` statement awaits a Lean proof of the hook-length formula. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.dim_validated_le12","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.dim_validated_le12","kind":"theorem","line":973,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L973-L979","doc":"**Dimension certificate (sorry-free).** `Σ_{λ⊢n} dim(λ)² = n!` for every `n ≤ 12` (the\nRSK sum-of-squares-of-dimensions identity).  Kernel `decide` over the enumerated partitions;\nthis certifies that `dimHLF` is the genuine `#SYT(λ)` — a floor-rounded value would break the\nequality. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.identityB_rhs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.identityB_rhs","kind":"def","line":969,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L969-L970","doc":"**(B) right side** `n! · binom(n,2)` (built in `ℕ`, so the statement carries no division). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.identityB_lhs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.identityB_lhs","kind":"def","line":965,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L965-L967","doc":"**(B) left side** `Σ_{λ⊢n} dim(λ)² · Σ_{c∈λ} c(c)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.partitionsOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.partitionsOf","kind":"def","line":962,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L962-L963","doc":"All integer partitions of `n` (weakly-decreasing `List ℕ`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.partsFuel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.partsFuel","kind":"def","line":950,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L950-L960","doc":"Fuel-based partition enumerator: all weakly-decreasing partitions of `target` with parts\nin `[1, cap]`.  **Structurally** recursive on `fuel` (no well-founded obligation); a partition\nof `n` has at most `n` parts, so `fuel = n` always suffices (`partitionsOf`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.dimHLF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.dimHLF","kind":"def","line":944,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L944-L948","doc":"**Hook-length-formula dimension** `dim(λ) = n!/∏_c h_c` (Frame–Robinson–Thrall).  `∏ h_c`\ndivides `n!` exactly, so the `ℕ` division is the honest integer `#SYT(λ)`; the exactness is\ncertified downstream by `dim_validated_le12` (`Σ_λ dim(λ)² = n!`, the RSK sum-of-squares),\nwhich would fail were any value floor-rounded. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.prodHooks","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.prodHooks","kind":"def","line":936,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L936-L942","doc":"`∏_{c∈λ} h_c`, the product of hook lengths (hook `h(i,j) = (λ_i−j)+(colLen j−i)−1`, the\nsame hook used by `sumSqHooks`).  Denominator of the Frame–Robinson–Thrall dimension. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.jm_identity_coeff_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.jm_identity_coeff_two","kind":"theorem","line":909,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L909-L922","doc":"**Identity (B), Jucys–Murphy core (sorry-free).** The Plancherel mean of the\nsquared-content sum equals the identity coefficient of the central element\n`p₂(X) = Σ_{k=1}^n X_k²` of `ℂ[S_n]` (each `X_k` a Jucys–Murphy element), namely\n`Σ_{k=1}^n (k−1) = Σ_{k<n} k`, and that coefficient is `binom(n,2)` — i.e.\n`(Σ_{k<n} k)·2 = n(n−1)`.  Here is that arithmetic core, proved outright (Gauss). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sumSqHooks_eq_sumSqContents_add_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sumSqHooks_eq_sumSqContents_add_sq","kind":"theorem","line":820,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L820-L905","doc":"**Identity (A), general (proved sorry-free).** For a weakly-decreasing\npartition `l`, `Σ_c h_c² = Σ_c c(c)² + n²`.  Machine-checked for all `n ≤ 9`\n(`identityA_verified_le9`), exhaustively in Python for `n ≤ 22`, and now proved\nfor **all** partitions here.\n\nProof (β-set / arm-leg, audit doc §\"Proof of (A)\").  Bridge the ℕ hook square to its\nℤ form on cells (`hook_eq`), clear the `6` with `mul_left_cancel₀`, and expand\n`H² = P²+Q²+1+2PQ−2P−2Q` (`P = λ_i−j`, `Q = colLen j−i`) into nine cell sums (`hsum`).\nEach cell sum has a row form discharged above:\n* `P²`,`P` — row reflection (`cellP_sq_eq`, `cellP_eq`);\n* `Q²`,`Q` — Fubini transpose (`cell_fubini`, via `colLen_duality`) then the K-moment\n  row forms (`cellQ_sq_eq`, `cellQ_eq`);\n* the `λ·colLen` cross term — λ-weighted min-sum (`cellAC_eq`), which contributes the\n  `+ n²`; the `j·colLen` cross term — j-weighted K2 (`cellBC_eq`);\n* the `λ·i`, `j·i`, and constant sums — direct (`hT5`, `hT7`, `hT3`).\nThe two `6·n²` scalars cancel and the nine rows collapse to the content cubic by\n`ring`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.cellBC_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.cellBC_eq","kind":"theorem","line":799,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L799-L818","doc":"`BC` cross piece `Σ_c j·colLen j` (j-weighted K2; `2·` clears the inner Gauss sum). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.cellAC_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.cellAC_eq","kind":"theorem","line":783,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L783-L797","doc":"`AC` cross piece `Σ_c λ_i·colLen j` (λ-weighted min-sum). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.cellQ_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.cellQ_eq","kind":"theorem","line":767,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L767-L781","doc":"`Q` term (`cell_fubini` + column reflection + K-moment row forms). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.cellQ_sq_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.cellQ_sq_eq","kind":"theorem","line":747,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L747-L765","doc":"`Q²` term (`cell_fubini` + column reflection + K-moment row forms). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.cellP_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.cellP_eq","kind":"theorem","line":740,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L740-L745","doc":"`P` term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.cellP_sq_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.cellP_sq_eq","kind":"theorem","line":732,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L732-L738","doc":"`P²` term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sum_colLen_cube_row_int","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sum_colLen_cube_row_int","kind":"theorem","line":719,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L719-L723","doc":"ℤ form of the K3 row moment. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sum_colLen_sq_row_int","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sum_colLen_sq_row_int","kind":"theorem","line":713,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L713-L717","doc":"ℤ form of the K2 row moment. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sum_colLen_parts_int","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sum_colLen_parts_int","kind":"theorem","line":707,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L707-L711","doc":"ℤ form of the K1 row moment. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.two_mul_sum_range_refl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.two_mul_sum_range_refl","kind":"theorem","line":693,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L693-L705","doc":"Reflected linear sum: `2·Σ_{j<M}((M:ℤ)−j) = M(M+1)` (the `Σ_{m=1}^M m` form). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.six_mul_sum_range_refl_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.six_mul_sum_range_refl_sq","kind":"theorem","line":679,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L679-L691","doc":"Reflected square sum: `6·Σ_{j<M}((M:ℤ)−j)² = M(M+1)(2M+1)` (the `Σ_{m=1}^M m²` form). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.two_mul_sum_lambda_min","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.two_mul_sum_lambda_min","kind":"theorem","line":641,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L641-L677","doc":"**λ-weighted min-sum (sorry-free).** `2·Σ_i λ_i·Σ_k min(λ_i,λ_k) = Σ_i(2i+1)λ_i² + n²`\n(over `ℕ`).  Uses the pointwise identity `(a+b)·min(a,b) = min(a,b)² + a·b` + symmetry,\ncollapsing to `antitone_f_min_sum` (`f = ·²`) and `(Σλ)² = n²` — no per-row split needed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sum_j_colLen_sq_row_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sum_j_colLen_sq_row_form","kind":"theorem","line":633,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L633-L639","doc":"**`j`-weighted K2 as a row form (sorry-free).** `Σ_j j·colLen(j)² = Σ_i (2i+1)·Σ_{j<λ_i} j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sum_j_colLen_sq_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sum_j_colLen_sq_eq","kind":"theorem","line":620,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L620-L631","doc":"`Σ_c c·colLen(c)² = Σ_{i,k} Σ_{j<min(λ_i,λ_k)} j` (`j`-weighted analogue of K2). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sum_ite_lt_id","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sum_ite_lt_id","kind":"theorem","line":606,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L606-L618","doc":"`j`-weighted `<`-indicator sum: `Σ_{j<a}(if j<b then j else 0) = Σ_{j<min a b} j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.per_i_min_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.per_i_min_split","kind":"theorem","line":592,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L592-L604","doc":"Per-row min split: `Σ_{k<r} min(a i,a k) = (i+1)·a i + Σ_{i<k<r} a k` (antitone, `i<r`).\nThe tail `Σ_{i<k<r} a k`, weighted by `a i` and summed, becomes `Σ_{i<k} a i a k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.antitone_f_min_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.antitone_f_min_sum","kind":"theorem","line":571,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L571-L590","doc":"General `f`-min-sum: `Σ_{i,k<r} f(min(a i,a k)) = Σ_{i<r}(2i+1)·f(a i)` for antitone `a`.\nGeneralizes `antitone_min_sum` (`f = id`); also gives `Σ_j j·colLen(j)²` with `f = m↦\\binom m2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sum_colLen_cube_row_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sum_colLen_cube_row_form","kind":"theorem","line":556,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L556-L562","doc":"**`K3` as a row form (sorry-free).** `Σ_j colLen(j)³ = Σ_i (3i²+3i+1)·λ_i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sum_colLen_cube_eq_sum_min3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sum_colLen_cube_eq_sum_min3","kind":"theorem","line":530,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L530-L554","doc":"`Σ_c colLen(c)³ = Σ_{x,i,m} min3(λ_x,λ_i,λ_m)` (cube each `colLen` into row-indicators,\n`sum_comm` the column index inward, then the triple-indicator/`min` count).  Right-associated\n`min` to match the natural product expansion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.antitone_min3_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.antitone_min3_sum","kind":"theorem","line":478,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L478-L528","doc":"**Triple min order-split (sorry-free).** For an antitone sequence,\n`Σ_{i,k,m<r} min(min(a i,a k),a m) = Σ_{i<r}(3i²+3i+1)·a i` — each new index `n` is the\nsmallest, so all 7 \"shell\" tuples touching it contribute `a n`\n(`(n+1)³−n³ = 3n²+3n+1`).  Row closed form of the column moment `Σ_j colLen(j)³`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sum_range_getD_eq_sz","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sum_range_getD_eq_sz","kind":"theorem","line":467,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L467-L476","doc":"The size `n = Σ λ_i` is the `Finset.range` sum of the parts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sum_colLen_eq_sum_parts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sum_colLen_eq_sum_parts","kind":"theorem","line":457,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L457-L465","doc":"**`K1` as a row form (sorry-free).** `Σ_j colLen(j) = Σ_i λ_i` (both count cells). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sum_colLen_sq_row_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sum_colLen_sq_row_form","kind":"theorem","line":450,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L450-L455","doc":"**`K2` as a row form (sorry-free).** `Σ_j colLen(j)² = Σ_i (2i+1)·λ_i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sum_colLen_sq_eq_sum_min","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sum_colLen_sq_eq_sum_min","kind":"theorem","line":433,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L433-L448","doc":"`Σ_j colLen(j)² = Σ_{i,k} min(λ_i, λ_k)` (expand each `colLen` to row-indicators,\n`Finset.sum_comm` the column index inward, then the indicator/`min` count). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.indicator_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.indicator_mul","kind":"theorem","line":427,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L427-L431","doc":"Product of two `<`-indicators is the indicator of the `min`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.antitone_min_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.antitone_min_sum","kind":"theorem","line":406,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L406-L425","doc":"**Min order-split (sorry-free).** For an antitone sequence,\n`Σ_{i,k<r} min(a i, a k) = Σ_{i<r} (2i+1)·a i` — each new index `n` contributes a full\nrow + column of `a n` (it is the smallest, so the min on the new cross terms).  This is the\nrow closed form of the column moment `Σ_j colLen(j)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.getD_antitone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.getD_antitone","kind":"theorem","line":395,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L395-L404","doc":"For a weakly-decreasing list, `getD` is antitone in the index. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sum_colLen_eq_sum_min","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sum_colLen_eq_sum_min","kind":"theorem","line":377,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L377-L387","doc":"**Atomic min-sum bridge (sorry-free).** The row sum of column-heights over a row equals\nthe min-sum: `Σ_{j<λ_i} colLen(j) = Σ_k min(λ_i, λ_k)`.  Gateway to the arm·leg cross term\n(its `Σ_{i,k} λ_i·min(λ_i,λ_k)` closed form, via an order-split on `λ_i` vs `λ_k`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sum_indicator_lt_eq_min","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sum_indicator_lt_eq_min","kind":"theorem","line":368,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L368-L375","doc":"`Σ_{j<a} [j < b] = min a b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.colLen_eq_indicator_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.colLen_eq_indicator_sum","kind":"theorem","line":357,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L357-L366","doc":"`colLen` as a sum of row-indicators: `colLen(j) = Σ_k [j < λ_k]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.cell_fubini","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.cell_fubini","kind":"theorem","line":334,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L334-L347","doc":"**Fubini transpose (sorry-free).** A row-indexed cell sum equals the column-indexed one,\nfor any cell function `g`.  This is the (L1)/(Lal) 2-D reindex, via `Finset.sum_comm'` and the\ncell-membership duality.  The leg terms of `Σ_c h²` become per-column sums under it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.getD_le_headD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.getD_le_headD","kind":"theorem","line":316,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L316-L332","doc":"Every part is `≤` the first (largest) part, for a weakly-decreasing partition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.colLen_le_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.colLen_le_length","kind":"theorem","line":311,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L311-L314","doc":"`colLen ≤ length` (a column has at most as many cells as there are rows). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.colLen_duality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.colLen_duality","kind":"theorem","line":283,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L283-L309","doc":"**Cell-membership duality (sorry-free).** For a weakly-decreasing partition, row `i`\nreaches column `j` iff column `j` reaches row `i`: `i < colLen(j) ↔ j < λ_i`.  The gateway\nto the Fubini transpose; an induction on the parts using the column-empty lemma at the head. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.colLen_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.colLen_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":274,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L274-L281","doc":"If every part is `≤ j`, column `j` is empty. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.colLen_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.colLen_cons","kind":"theorem","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L267-L272","doc":"`colLen` recursion on a cons: prepending `a` adds a column-`j` cell iff `j < a`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.two_mul_sumLegs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.two_mul_sumLegs","kind":"theorem","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L246-L256","doc":"**Leg-linear side, closed form (sorry-free).** `2·Σ_c l(c) = Σ_j colLen(j)(colLen(j)−1)`,\nthe column transpose of `two_mul_sumArms`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.six_mul_sumSqLegs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.six_mul_sumSqLegs","kind":"theorem","line":234,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L234-L244","doc":"**Leg-square side, closed form (sorry-free).** `6·Σ_c l(c)² = Σ_j colLen(j)(colLen(j)−1)(2·colLen(j)−1)`,\nthe column transpose of `six_mul_sumSqArms` (reflect each column's leg sum onto `Σ_{k<colLen j} k²`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.two_mul_sumArms","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.two_mul_sumArms","kind":"theorem","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L222-L232","doc":"**Arm-linear side, closed form (sorry-free).** `2·Σ_c a(c) = Σ_i λ_i(λ_i−1)`,\nreflecting each row's arm sum onto the Gauss sum `Σ_{k<λ_i} k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.six_mul_sumSqArms","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.six_mul_sumSqArms","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L210-L220","doc":"**Arm-square side, closed form (sorry-free).** `6·Σ_c a(c)² = Σ_i λ_i(λ_i−1)(2λ_i−1)`,\nreflecting each row's arm sum onto `Σ_{k<λ_i} k²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.six_mul_sumSqContents","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.six_mul_sumSqContents","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L181-L197","doc":"**Content side of (A), closed form (sorry-free).** The full squared-content sum\n`Σ_c c(c)²` equals an explicit cubic summed over the rows — no hook-length, β-set, or\nJucys–Murphy infrastructure.  Multiplying by `6` clears the `Σ k²` / `Σ k`\ndenominators: `6·Σ_c c(c)² = Σ_i [λ_i(λ_i−1)(2λ_i−1) − 6i·λ_i(λ_i−1) + 6λ_i·i²]`,\nthe rows indexed `0 ≤ i < length` with `λ_i = l.getD i 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.six_mul_sum_range_content_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.six_mul_sum_range_content_sq","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L166-L179","doc":"**Per-row content-square closed form (sorry-free).** For a row of length `m` at\nrow index `i`, `6·Σ_{j<m}(j−i)² = m(m−1)(2m−1) − 6i·m(m−1) + 6m·i²`.  This is the\ncontent analogue of `six_mul_sum_range_sq`: the `Σ k²` cubic and the Gauss `Σ k`\nassembled with the `−i` content shift. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.list_range_map_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.list_range_map_sum","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L156-L164","doc":"Bridge a `List.range`-mapped sum to the corresponding `Finset.range` sum, so the\nclosed-form algebra lemmas apply to the computable `List`-based models above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.two_mul_sum_range_int","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.two_mul_sum_range_int","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L138-L147","doc":"**Gauss sum over `ℤ` (sorry-free).** `2·Σ_{k<N} k = N(N−1)`.  The linear companion\nof `six_mul_sum_range_sq`; feeds the arm/content linear pieces below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.six_mul_sum_range_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.six_mul_sum_range_sq","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L126-L136","doc":"**Building block for the general (A) proof — sum of squares (sorry-free).**\n`6·Σ_{k<N} k² = N(N−1)(2N−1)`.  Together with the Gauss sum `Σ_{k<N} k` it gives the\nsingle-row content closed form `Σ_{j<λ_i}(j−i)²` in the β-set/arm-leg assembly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.identityA_verified_le9","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.identityA_verified_le9","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L121-L124","doc":"**(A) for all partitions `n ≤ 9`** — sorry-free kernel `decide` over `allPartsLE9`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.allPartsLE9","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.allPartsLE9","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L102-L119","doc":"All integer partitions for `1 ≤ n ≤ 9` (96 of them), as weakly-decreasing lists. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sumLegs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sumLegs","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L90-L94","doc":"`Σ_{cells} leg(c)` with leg `l(i,j) = colLen(j) − 1 − i`, summed by columns.\nCarries the `2l` cross term of `h² = (a+l+1)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sumSqLegs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sumSqLegs","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L84-L88","doc":"`Σ_{cells} leg(c)²` with leg `l(i,j) = colLen(j) − 1 − i`, summed by **columns**\n`j = 0 … λ_1 − 1` (`λ_1 = l.headD 0`).  The `l²` term of `h² = (a+l+1)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sumArms","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sumArms","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L78-L82","doc":"`Σ_{cells} arm(c)` with arm `a(i,j) = λ_i − 1 − j`.  Carries the `2a` cross term of\n`h² = (a+l+1)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sumSqArms","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sumSqArms","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L72-L76","doc":"`Σ_{cells} arm(c)²` with arm `a(i,j) = λ_i − 1 − j` (cells of row `i` are\n`j = 0 … λ_i − 1`).  One of the six terms of the hook square `h² = (a+l+1)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sz","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sz","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L69-L70","doc":"Size `n = Σ λ_i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sumSqContents","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sumSqContents","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L62-L67","doc":"`Σ_{cells} c(c)²` with content `c(i,j) = j − i`.  The inner binder is annotated\n`(j : ℕ)` so the cast `(j : ℤ)` lives inside a single `ℕ → ℤ` map (matching `sumSqHooks`),\nkeeping the def reducible for the closed-form lemmas below; the values are unchanged. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sumSqHooks","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sumSqHooks","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L54-L60","doc":"`Σ_{cells} h(c)²` with hook `h(i,j) = (λ_i − j) + (colLen j − i) − 1`\n(`0`-indexed `i,j`; for a weakly-decreasing `l` and a genuine cell both summands are\n`≥ 1`, so the `ℕ` subtraction is exact). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.colLen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.colLen","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIContentDecomposition.lean#L50-L52","doc":"Column length of a partition (a weakly-decreasing `List ℕ`) at column `j`:\nthe number of parts exceeding `j` (`= λ'_{j+1}`, 0-indexed). ","signatureChunk":0}]}